57bm-i13"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257bm-i13"],"id":"long.record-257bm-i13","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.122 (Two-sided dyadic bounds)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.122, p. 78, label record:257bm-i13","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Under the local hypothesis excluding the specified three middle cells and imposing the right-pulse bound, induction (base case at row 5 verified by direct computation) propagates it to the universal two-sided bound\n$$\n\\forall s\\ge5,\\quad \\min(\\mathrm{rem}(s),\\ \\mathrm{overshoot}(s)) \\;\\le\\; 2^s.\n$$\nThis conditional bound says that at least one of the remainder and the adjacent overshoot is at most $2^s$. It does not assert that both are at most $2^s$; that stronger assertion would replace the minimum by a maximum. It is not needed for the charge bound at an actual upper reset: Proposition 6.80 obtains that bound directly from the upper-reset identity. Applying the inductive argument to another recurrence would require its own transition and separation estimates.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/long.record-257bm-i13","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/long.record-257bm-i13","id":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-i13%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_two_sided_dyadic_bound%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-i13%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_two_sided_dyadic_bound%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR